  <!-- Headline -->
  <h2>What Actually Makes eSIM Card Different</h2>
  <p>
    eSIM Card's real difference is how granular its own country pages are. Most providers on this site sell a handful of preset bundles per country: pick a data size, pick a length, done. eSIM Card's United States page alone lists roughly 30 combinations: seven fixed-data tiers (1GB, 3GB, 5GB, 10GB, 20GB, 50GB, 100GB) each sold at several different validity windows from 3 to 90 days, plus two separate unlimited tiers, "Unlimited" and "Unlimited Plus," running anywhere from 1 to 30 days. If you know exactly how much data and how many days you need, there's a plan sized for that instead of rounding up to whatever bundle a competitor happens to offer.
  </p>
  <p>
    eSIM Card also runs a couple of things most data-only competitors don't: a separate Data + Voice eSIM product line, and a standalone virtual phone number add-on starting around $2.40, both sold inside the same app as its regular data plans. That's a similar idea to what <a href="/alosim/">AloSIM</a> does through its Hushed partnership, but here the number is its own paid purchase rather than something bundled free with a data plan.
  </p>

  <!-- Codes -->
