  <div class="content-faq">
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>What is the best code right now</h3>
      <p><strong>ESIM10</strong>: 10% off any eSIM Card plan. It's a public code advertised directly on eSIM Card's own homepage, not one of ours.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Does eSIM Card sell unlimited plans</h3>
      <p>Yes, two tiers per country: "Unlimited" and "Unlimited Plus," each available at several validity lengths, on top of the regular fixed-GB plans. eSIM Card's own site doesn't spell out exactly what separates the two tiers beyond price.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Is eSIM Card's unlimited data actually unlimited</h3>
      <p>Per eSIM Card's own fair-use wording, unlimited bundles get "an allowed limit of data at full speed per 24 hours and thereafter unlimited data at lower speeds." The page confirms tethering/hotspot works on these plans, but doesn't publish the actual GB figure for that daily full-speed allowance the way some competitors do.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Can I get a phone number with eSIM Card</h3>
      <p>Yes, as a separate virtual phone number add-on starting around $2.40, purchased inside the same app as the data eSIMs rather than bundled in for free.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Can I get a refund</h3>
      <p>Rarely, once an eSIM is installed or used. eSIM Card's own refund policy describes eSIMs as fundamentally non-refundable, with exceptions limited to narrow cases like a genuine coverage failure or a technical fault with zero data consumed, claimed within 30 days of purchase.</p>
    </div>
